<title>MEXICO: Arancia-Corn Products to operate own gas pipeline.</title>
<headline>Arancia-Corn Products to operate own gas pipeline.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arancia-Corn Products, a maker of corn derivatives, has obtained permission to construct and operate its own natural gas pipeline to meet its needs at the San Juan del Rio plant in Queretero state, the Energy Regulatory Commission (CRE) said Monday.</p>
<p>The CRE said Arancia-Corn Products is the first company to obtain such permission in Mexico.</p>
<p>The gas duct will be one foot (30 cm) in diameter and 2.7 miles (4.3 km) long and is exepcted to be operational early next year, the CRE said.</p>
<p>-- Veronica Galan, Guadalajara bureau, (523) 817-0440</p>
